s learn that palliative care is appropriate across serious illness, not only at the final days of life.", "children": [{"id": "2c0f5d2f-6e6b-4ad3-a127-c6cf302fca48", "type": "concept", "title": "Symptom assessment and comfort"}, {"id": "7c463a52-0740-425f-92d1-bdf753399725", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality of life and goal-concordant care"}, {"id": "fe245076-b629-4545-89a3-0b99151df7aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Interdisciplinary palliative team roles"}]}, {"id": "48a9ee4d-b5fa-4a7f-adec-bf91b0697b9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advance care planning", "description": "This subtopic prepares students to support documentation and conversations before crisis decisions.", "children": [{"id": "9f058fc2-0c4f-4813-8504-c7100c600d84", "type": "concept", "title": "Advance directives and surrogate decision-makers"}, {"id": "5cd30760-8cb3-4028-be48-674be3ff6ce5", "type": "concept", "title": "Code status and POLST/MOLST concepts"}, {"id": "0df62dee-6178-4ec6-80de-312e75179d92", "type": "concept", "title": "Values, culture, spirituality, and family dynamics"}]}, {"id": "f42dd9d6-fb1d-4c7d-baba-24f143f25aeb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "End-of-life nursing care", "description": "Students learn to care for the patient and family through dying, grief, and bereavement.", "children": [{"id": "43a14ec0-e026-42e0-aa99-ed4ed8fa60cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Pain, dyspnea, agitation, secretions, and comfort measures"}, {"id": "bcd307d3-d3ad-40a7-bab1-9b94e19c26d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Signs of active dying"}, {"id": "21f9a379-4bf5-4545-896b-96607fe7057e", "type": "concept", "title": "Family presence, rituals, and bereavement support"}]}]}, {"id": "c34be89d-6e54-42ee-90a8-0259cfbe0da4", "type": "topic", "title": "Care settings, transitions, aging in place, long-term care, and caregiver support", "description": "Coordinate care across home, hospital, rehab, assisted living, skilled nursing, and community settings.", "children": [{"id": "8b098907-5801-4a95-8c42-d6f205dd0c4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuum of older-adult care", "description": "Students learn how risks and nursing priorities change across home, acute care, rehab, assisted living, and skilled nursing.", "children": [{"id": "9cd65203-d2a8-4bb7-ae45-afec5c439b63", "type": "concept", "title": "Hospital, rehab, SNF, assisted living, long-term care, and hospice"}, {"id": "2b0fc8f8-f0fa-4914-89da-c14093d16e31", "type": "concept", "title": "Aging in place and home health"}, {"id": "4b518882-e1c1-4b16-a223-8e5064320598", "type": "concept", "title": "Community resources and benefits navigation"}]}, {"id": "4701174f-763d-475e-b331-d0af09ed182b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transitions of care", "description": "This subtopic focuses on the vulnerable handoffs where older adults often experience medication errors, falls, and readmissions.", "children": [{"id": "11ef09a8-6aac-49ab-a15d-1eadc1ba6c61", "type": "concept", "title": "Discharge readiness and teach-back"}, {"id": "a66db20f-d515-4a42-9032-4b9cb998f317", "type": "concept", "title": "Medication and follow-up reconciliation"}, {"id": "af7529e1-c3c0-4fbc-af1d-a19ce87beb15", "type": "concept", "title": "Red flags, return precautions, and care coordination"}]}, {"id": "e12f1642-3ee6-46d8-b8c3-13365dfb16d9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Caregiver support", "description": "Students learn that caregiver capacity is part of the care plan.", "children": [{"id": "095a8d86-f3df-42d7-b80b-799346858ab9", "type": "concept", "title": "Caregiver assessment and burden"}, {"id": "56182b89-2b5c-4f0f-a552-ddb795ad638c", "type": "concept", "title": "Education, respite, and community supports"}, {"id": "4a6e0a4a-d68b-4c7d-b378-8a5b4448f196", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety planning and caregiver inclusion"}]}]}, {"id": "06c2c4d6-ff48-4457-b417-41f92e791880", "type": "topic", "title": "Elder abuse, ethics, legal issues, capacity, and advocacy", "description": "Protect vulnerable older adults while respecting autonomy, consent, capacity, justice, and professional duties.", "children": [{"id": "5d0d4332-948d-41e3-8ff0-3755f91caf65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Elder mistreatment recognition", "description": "Students learn to identify and respond to abuse, neglect, exploitation, and self-neglect.", "children": [{"id": "63e479c3-9cb1-4b37-9d74-def7dc68369d", "type": "concept", "title": "Physical, emotional, sexual, financial abuse, and neglect"}, {"id": "ad9b671a-ff4a-4783-b34d-3865d12817dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Warning signs and risk factors"}, {"id": "d4766c3e-1219-4aec-9774-72f41e6d6ae0", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation and mandated reporting concepts"}]}, {"id": "bd98f2d1-0df1-45f3-bead-95800dc61578", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capacity, consent, and autonomy", "description": "This subtopic balances safety with respect for older adults' rights and preferences.", "children": [{"id": "9babdc5e-959e-46f3-b07f-25ce0e738904", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision-making capacity versus legal competency"}, {"id": "5e8b3958-fca6-475b-a8bf-c288f4f5b886", "type": "concept", "title": "Supported decision-making"}, {"id": "9b7b1ef4-0194-4622-b3bc-cb7f1a9d5e25", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk tolerance, refusal of care, and least restrictive alternatives"}]}, {"id": "e3a6bce4-0aea-487e-a679-f01dc89fdc72", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical and legal nursing responsibilities", "description": "Students learn to advocate in complex situations involving vulnerability, family conflict, and systems constraints.", "children": [{"id": "c49ff247-8271-4f6a-918c-798977c9d8a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Beneficence, nonmaleficence, autonomy, and justice"}, {"id": "ad126ef4-3f26-4de4-8880-83a92e449f7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and privacy"}, {"id": "f288c00b-9257-46e9-89be-31d92de079ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Guardianship, advance directives, and professional boundaries"}]}]}, {"id": "cee53dd2-73ca-49e8-9033-2ee474f5e2d5", "type": "topic", "title": "Population health, interprofessional teamwork, evidence-based protocols, and quality improvement", "description": "Use gerontological evidence, community resources, team-based care, and quality metrics to improve older-adult outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "5d0b0417-e899-444c-b618-def0897c6e42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Population and community aging", "description": "Students learn to view older-adult care through public health, social determinants, and community design.", "children": [{"id": "9704d220-6f9e-479e-9e15-822cad734627", "type": "concept", "title": "Aging demographics and disparities"}, {"id": "ced60088-066f-46c9-9ad0-5fb3aa6a46a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Social isolation, transportation, housing, and food security"}, {"id": "55708088-db30-43a4-be4f-25aa12810fd6", "type": "concept", "title": "Healthy People, CDC, and local aging resources"}]}, {"id": "9aa08320-3b9f-4ebf-a147-01ff1fee45ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interprofessional geriatric care", "description": "This subtopic highlights team roles that preserve function and prevent fragmented care.", "children": [{"id": "37e4ce34-8104-40ac-93af-a2895b3713fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Nursing, medicine, pharmacy, PT, OT, social work, nutrition, and chaplaincy"}, {"id": "70789599-64e0-44ee-86f8-e542c63df671", "type": "concept", "title": "Team communication and care conferences"}, {"id": "0d700805-32df-41cd-989f-99d99d86e842", "type": "concept", "title": "Care plans built around patient goals"}]}, {"id": "bed89dcc-de3d-4933-b1bf-f05e22ac812d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence-based protocols and quality improvement", "description": "Students learn to translate geriatric evidence into safer systems of care.", "children": [{"id": "968f632b-f255-4b6c-bce8-c977e998b53f", "type": "concept", "title": "Falls, delirium, pressure injury, medication safety, and transitions metrics"}, {"id": "3113721e-baa8-4c52-afea-6b8d85af7999", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality indicators and root-cause thinking"}, {"id": "aa4a3229-19f8-4340-a59a-5ca0bd4b4770", "type": "concept", "title": "Small tests of change and outcome tracking"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$gerjson$::jsonb,
